5. I reversed the ACH (PAY0002) so that only the wire, the method you preferred, would stand. The reversal came back as \"reversed.\"\n\n**Current state:**\n- **PAY0001 (wire, $4,676.43): sent.** This is the intended payment, and INV-34721 is marked paid.\n- **PAY0002 (ACH, $4,676.43): unclear.** The reversal said it worked, but the payment list still shows it as \"sent,\" even after a second check.\n\n**What needs to happen:** someone should check with the bank or treasury that the $4,676.43 ACH (PAY0002) was actually pulled back. If it wasn't, Harbor Logistics has been paid twice and the extra $4,676.43 needs to be recovered from them. I didn't try the reversal again because I couldn't tell what it would do.\n\nI didn't touch the other invoices. INV-73032 ($8,941.78) is still a draft awaiting approval, and INV-10769 was already paid.", "type": "text"}]}]}